<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="CH7x2016-en-ab262959" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Translation of  into (English)</title><editor role="translator">AI - Gemini</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title/>2025</bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#CH7x2016"><title xml:lang="och"/></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2025-10-16T19:51:06.784+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="CH7x2016-start"><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.37" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">Thereupon it was named thus.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.38" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">To the south is Mount Xǔ Yóu,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.39" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">tall and imposing, cut off on all four sides.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.40" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">To its north is the River Yǐng.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.41" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">Yáo employed Xǔ Yóu,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.42" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">the place where he resided still has an altar.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.43" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">Formerly, Prince Jìn, the crown prince of King Líng of Zhōu, loved to play the sheng (mouth organ),</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.44" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">composing melodies like the call of the phoenix,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.45" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">and wandered between the Yī and Luò Rivers.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.46" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">The Daoist Fú Qiū Gōng took him up to Mount Sōng,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.47" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">for more than thirty years,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.48" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">he traveled back and forth to Mount Gōu Shì.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.49" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">Mount Gōu Shì is located nearby, to the west of Mount Sōng.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.50" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">During the Hàn Dynasty, there was a Daoist priest</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.51" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">who brought seeds of the palm tree from a foreign country</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.52" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">and planted them at the western foot of Mount Sōng Gāo.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.53" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">There were four trees,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.54" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">different from other trees,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.55" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">flowering three times a year,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-104a.56" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">with white, fragrant and beautiful blossoms."</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">Two Chambers Three Platforms</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">Two Chambers,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">refers to Mount Tài Shì and Mount Shǎo Shì,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">already detailed in the narrative.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">Three Platforms Mountain,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">the name was established by Emperor Wǔ of the Hàn Dynasty,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">located on Mount Sōng,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">the matter has already been detailed in the narrative.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">Divine Peak Heavenly Garrison</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">The "Book of Odes" says:</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">"Lofty is Mount Sōng,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">towering to the heavens.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_005-105a.14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-10-16T19:55:06.88+09:00">From lofty peaks descends the divine,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-70a.7" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">When a bell is suspended from a horizontal beam and set up,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-70a.8" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">a *jūnzǐ* (gentleman) hearing its sound thinks of military officials."</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-70a.9" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Wáng Zǐnián's (王子年) *Shíyí Jì* (拾遺記) says:</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-70a.10" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">"When Emperor Zhuānxū (顓頊) was in power,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-70a.11" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">those with civil virtue were bestowed with bells and *qìng* (磬, lithophones),</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-70a.12" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">and those with martial virtue were bestowed with shields and spears."</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.1" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.2" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Left three, Right five.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.3" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Dài Yánzhī's (戴延之) *Xīzhēng Jì* (西征記) says:</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.4" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">"In front of the Dàjí Diàn (大極殿, Hall of Great Ultimate) in Luòyáng (洛陽),</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.5" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">there were three bronze bells on each side, facing each other.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.6" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">The large ones measured thirty-two *wéi* (圍, girths),</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.7" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">and the small ones measured twenty-five *wéi*."</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.8" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">*Hán Shī Wàichuán* (韓詩外傳, Han's Outer Commentary on the Odes) says:</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.9" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">"In ancient times, the Son of Heaven [Emperor]</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.10" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">had five bells on his left and right.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.11" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">When he was about to go out, he would strike the golden bell,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-71a.12" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">and all the (other) bells would resonate with it."</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.1" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.2" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Xuánchóng (旋蟲, Circling Worms), Ràoshòu (繞獸, Coiling Beasts)</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.3" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">"Xuánchóng" has already been discussed in the preceding narrative.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.4" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Lù Huì's (陸翽) *Yè Zhōng Jì* (鄴中記, Records of Ye) says:</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.5" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">"There were four bronze bells,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.6" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">shaped like a *duó* (鐸, large handbell).</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.7" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">They were two *zhàng* (丈) and eight *cùn* (寸) high.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.8" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">The outer width of the large face was one *zhàng* and two *chǐ* (尺),</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.9" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">and the outer width of the small face was seven *chǐ*.</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-72a.10" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Some were adorned with *jiāolóng* (蛟龍, flood dragons) or birds and beasts coiled on them."</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-73a.1" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-73a.2" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Fājīng (發鯨, Startling the Whale), Gòuzhì (雊雉, Crowing Pheasant)</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-73a.3" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Zhāng Héng's (張衡) *Xī Jīng Fù* (西京賦, Rhapsody on the Western Capital):</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-73a.4" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">"Striking the whale-bell,</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-73a.5" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">clanging the magnificent bells."</seg><seg corresp="#CH7x2016_CHANT_016-73a.6" generatedBy="bot-gemini-2.5-flash" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-03-28T20:17:36.417+09:00">Xuē Zōng's (薛綜) commentary says:</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>